        "original_id": "fa437fff-cfc3-589d-9b11-f4a41178515f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Francis Ford Coppola, Basil Dean, Mario Puzo, Al Pacino, Robert De Niro, Graham Cutts, Gracie Fields, Richard Dolman, Betty Shale\n- Works: The Godfather Part II, Looking on the Bright Side\n- Roles: film director, producer, screenwriter, film composer, actor, writer, theatrical producer/director\n\nFacts:\n- Basil Herbert Dean was born on 27 September 1888 and died on 22 April 1978.\n- Basil Herbert Dean was an English actor, writer, film producer, film director, and theatrical producer and director.\n- In 1932, Looking on the Bright Side was released as a British musical comedy film.\n- Looking on the Bright Side was directed by Graham Cutts and Basil Dean.\n- Looking on the Bright Side starred Gracie Fields, Richard Dolman, and Betty Shale.\n- Francis Ford Coppola was born on April 7, 1939.\n- Francis Ford Coppola, also credited as Francis Coppola, is a semi-retired American film director, producer, screenwriter, and film composer.\n- In 1974, The Godfather Part II was released as an American crime film.\n- The Godfather Part II was produced and directed by Francis Ford Coppola.\n- The Godfather Part II was written from a screenplay co-written by Francis Ford Coppola and Mario Puzo.\n- The Godfather Part II starred Al Pacino and Robert De Niro.",
